                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose: growth stall, runway & identity`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `It is 2 March 2026. Your largest competitor just raised <strong>€12M</strong> while Racine's growth flattened at <strong>€1.4M ARR</strong>. You hold <strong>€855K cash</strong> against <strong>€95K monthly burn</strong> — read the clock precisely. Before choosing capital, diagnose <em>why</em> growth stalled, state your true runway, and name the <strong>two identity attributes</strong> that must survive any growth path. Racine has turned away two clients on principle — that selectivity, and the team mission-fit it earns, are the moat funding terms can destroy.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Activate the network for resourcefulness`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Before you raise a euro, work the asset you already have. Camille's alumni cohort, two anchor-customer advisors and a sustainability-investor community can unlock <strong>€400–600K</strong> of resourcefulness value — three warm enterprise pilots, co-marketing, a shared senior engineer — that substitutes <em>relationship capital</em> for financial capital and reshapes the terms on every funding path. The tension is the founder's <strong>attention budget</strong>: time spent activating the network is time not spent fund-raising. Leverage it without starving the raise.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Choose the path & reconcile identity`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Decision time. The VC offers <strong>€6M at €24M</strong> — but with an “any-customer” clause and a <strong>2x liquidation preference</strong> that pull against the mission. Revenue-based finance gives <strong>€1.5M</strong>, slower but identity-preserving. The agri-corporate offers <strong>€2M + distribution</strong> — with exclusivity that would block your retail channel and a board seat. <em>Mid-quarter shock: the VC accelerates its deadline and the partner hardens the exclusivity demand.</em> Accept, renegotiate, or reject the strings — and protect identity-alignment without starving runway.`,
