                    sum_r4_hyper:           `Chased hyper-growth the resources couldn't carry.`,
                    sum_r4_weak:            `Plan partly sustainable.`,

                    insight_sustainable:    `Growing on purpose: you matched the financing instrument to the venture's ambition and identity, activated the network as a real growth engine, and set a rate Racine's resources can carry. ARR is heading credibly toward €3M, the runway is healthy, and the moat — mission selectivity and team mission-fit — is intact. Growth was a rate you chose, not a velocity that broke you.`,
                    insight_valuation_tunnel: `Valuation tunnel vision: you took the €6M at €24M and accepted the “any-customer” clause and the 2x preference. The valuation looked like a win, but identity-alignment collapsed from 82 toward 41 — mission-hired engineers left and an anchor customer cooled. The capital bought a number; it cost you the moat that produced the revenue in the first place.`,
                    insight_free_money:     `Free-money illusion: the agri-corporate's €2M and distribution were never free. The exclusivity blocked the retail channel that was 30% of your pipeline, and the board seat now vetoes your next raise. You traded independence for one customer's roadmap — the headline price was the cheap part.`,
                    insight_bootstrap_blind: `Identity purism: you protected the mission and the cap table but ignored the €12M competitor's war chest. ARR stayed flat near €1.4M while the rival outspent you on your own enterprise deals. Under-capitalisation is also a failure mode — there was a path that protected both identity and the market.`,
                    insight_unsustainable_rate: `Unsustainable velocity: you may have hit the number, but you chased a 3x rate your resources couldn't carry — burn climbed, the team strained, and identity-alignment took the hit. Growing “on purpose” is a rate you choose for what the venture can sustain, not the fastest pace you can force. The board can tell the difference between momentum and a plan.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed result: parts of the plan worked, but growth, runway, network and identity never fully converged on a sustainable rate. Enough seams remained for a board to question whether the next raise comes from strength.`,
                    insight_network_neglect: `Network neglected: you left €400–600K of resourcefulness value unused — warm pilots, co-marketing and shared hiring your cohort had offered. Those pilots would have strengthened your raise and your negotiating position. The network was a growth instrument, not a nicety.`,
                    insight_sales_delay:    `Over-conservatism on burn: delaying or skipping the €180K enterprise sales lead saved cash but slipped the pipeline a quarter — and every growth path assumed those deals closing this half. Protecting runway starved the growth the runway was for.`,
                    insight_channel_blocked: `The exclusivity clause blocked the retail channel that was 30% of your pipeline, capping ARR short of the €3M milestone. Strategic dependence is a hidden cost you pay every quarter after signing.`,
                    insight_runway_out:     `Runway ran thin: you reached the end of the window with under six months of cash, which means raising from desperation rather than strength. The clock was always the binding constraint.`,
                    insight_identity_lost:  `The moat dissolved: identity-alignment fell below the level at which customers trust you and mission-hired engineers stay. Once the trust and motivation that drive growth are gone, the capital that bought them cannot buy them back.`,
                    insight_too_slow:       `Identity intact and solvent — but ARR never reached the €3M milestone. You grew sustainably but too slowly to raise from strength next time, and a €12M-funded rival doesn't wait. Sustainable also has to mean fast enough.`,

                    hint_valuation_tunnel:  `You accepted the identity-violating VC terms — the moat is cracking. You can't rebuild identity-alignment past the cap now; focus the remaining rounds on retaining whoever's left and proving the growth was worth it.`,
                    hint_free_money:        `The partnership's exclusivity blocked your retail channel and the board seat constrains your next raise. ARR is capped below the milestone — the strings you didn't price are the bill now coming due.`,
